{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339026-question-concerning-spirit-allies-guides-for-new-age-dreamspeaker","id":1339026,"title":"Question concerning spirit allies/guides for New Age Dreamspeaker","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-02T11:26:10-07:00","id":1339026,"title":"Question concerning spirit allies/guides for New Age Dreamspeaker","content":"Greetings, guys!<br /> <br /> So, I'm dipping my foot into the vast pool of New Age spiritualism by playing a fortune teller type character as a Dreamspeaker (who really does much more than that, but represents herself as that to prevent suspicion and provide more coincidental effects) and I have plenty of spirit ideas, but I'm not sure if they have any cohesion.<br /> <br /> For example, her spirit practices range from beings as earthly as Deva (fairies) who order the natural realm, to extraterrestrial beings that live on the stars and other parts of the cosmos. But does it seem odd, even if I can fit it into her paradigm, for a mystic to also contact extraterrestrial beings (I assume that's more of an Etherite thing.)<br /> <br /> Essentially, I suppose I'm asking if it makes *sense* for my character to have a cacophony of inter-genre influences that she draws upon for spiritual inspiration and power. Secondly, how do you suggest I meld them if it does make sense? Could an example of invoking extraterrestrial spiritual energy involve gravity, or some sort of that sort? And what kind of chiminage would you imagine such beings would want?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T20:36:01-07:00","id":1339110,"title":"","content":"Well, this is the new Age times. Spirits are so last season. Neo-Pagans and Tech-Shamans are the rage, if Tech-Shamans can contact regular spirits + digital spirits theres no reason you couldn't know a few aliens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T00:38:14-07:00","id":1339136,"title":"","content":"Sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic. It stands to reason, ergo, that sufficiently strange aliens are indistinguishable from spirits. Beings that exist in other dimensions would certainly interact with our dimension in strange ways, because they obey different natural laws. By that same token, we interact with them in strange ways, and can use different methods - including high ritual and symbols - to manipulate them and curry favor.<br /> <br /> There's also Chaos Magick, which freely conflates Spirits, Aliens, and Thought Forms together. See also the works of Blue Fluke and their <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/bluefluke/gallery/52627976/the-psychonaut-field-manual\" target=\"_blank\">Psychonaut Field Manual</a>, a series of illustrated guides to (a form of) chaos magick. (Warning: very occasionally the manual is mildly NSFW). It's not too in-depth, but it has sections on dealing with Thought Forms and Spirits (and how they may or may not be the same thing).<br /> <br /> See also <a href=\"http://www.chaosmatrix.org/library/chaos/texts/model.html\" target=\"_blank\">this article</a> from 1991 by Frater U.'.D.'., concerning different models of magic. This is more about magical theory (or rather the different broad theories), rather than specific means of applying them. What's important to your character is how they envision what they're doing when they do magic. Is she coaxing unaware spiritual forces towards a specific goal? Is she trying to get aware entities from another world to do what she wants? Is she using information to give form (even being?) to undifferentiated potential from outside our universe (or exploiting information already put into place, by mortals or non-mortals)? Etc, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T00:52:47-07:00","id":1339139,"title":"","content":"Another thing to research: Franz Friedrich Anton Mezmer's theories of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Animal_magnetism\" target=\"_blank\">Animal Magnetism</a> (sometimes called Mezmerism), a scientific theory prevalent in the 19th century that was heavily co-opted by contemporary spiritualist movements. The idea states that living things have a kind of magnetic field, produced by &quot;vital fluids&quot; (the prevailing wisdom of the time didn't distinguish between energy fields and liquids; we see this with ideas like Phlogiston and early conceptions of electricity). These fields or vital fluids could be manipulated, either by way of magnets or by the movement of hands (using one's own magnetic field to influence others).<br /> <br /> Principally it was a medical discipline, but spiritualists, occultists, and charlatans ascribed powers of levitation, conjuration, and mind control to it (hence &quot;Mezmerism&quot; being synonymous with hypnotism). They also linked it to the world of spirits, as was the style of the time (spiritualists linked basically everything together, in pursuit of knowledge, power, and the alleviation of boredom).<br /> <br /> Because of its pseudo-scientific nature, Animal Magnetism makes good Focus fodder for both Dreamspeakers and Etherites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T06:47:38-07:00","id":1339166,"title":"","content":"Just want to say that the articles mentioned by Bluecho are amazing. Shame on you for not sharing this stuff earlier. <br /> <br /> Got any more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T07:54:16-07:00","id":1339179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339026-question-concerning-spirit-allies-guides-for-new-age-dreamspeaker?p=1339166#post1339166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just want to say that the articles mentioned by Bluecho are amazing. Shame on you for not sharing this stuff earlier.<br /> <br /> Got any more?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Not on topic, at least. It's been a while since I did research on occult subjects. I didn't even know Bluefluke released another edition of the Psychonaut Manual until I went looking for links. (The latest I had was from 2015).<br /> <br /> If I had some advice, though, I'd suggest looking up more material on 19th century spiritualism. There's a lot to explore there, because the degree to which occult subjects were part of the mainstream wouldn't be matched until the 60s. Many of the trends that New Age worked with were cribbed from that period. That and the Golden Dawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T08:41:44-07:00","id":1339191,"title":"","content":"Wow, Bluecho, this is great research fodder! Thank you.<br /> <br /> A lot of UFO-based New Age beliefs almost always involve \u201cchanneling\u201d a spirit/extraterrestrial being through a mortal vessel so they can speak. <br /> <br /> Also, as for the alien thing I want to go all the way with it: while she will have great reverence for earthly beings (Deva, animal spirits of wisdom, spirits of distance, positivity, cleansing etc) she will similarly have her eye on the cosmos. I can imagine her trying to send her voice through the gauntlet and towards Sirius B, the brightest star in the sky, to reach any light-aligned extraterrestrials that may be stationed there.<br /> <br /> In fact, there\u2019s a lot of people who actually believe that a mass intergalactic alliance of light beings actually exist, exhibit A:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.andromedacouncil.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.andromedacouncil.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.andromedacouncil.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.andromedacouncil.com/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Exhibit B:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.paoweb.com/gfmember.htm\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.paoweb.com/gfmtype1.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.paoweb.com/gfmember.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> PAO - Galactic Federation Members </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.paoweb.com/gfmember.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.paoweb.com/gfmember.htm </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If I wanted to represent those as Umbrood extraterrestrial spirits, how do you think I could best do that while still keeping within the dreamspeaker paradigm?<br /> <br /> And if I were to make a pact and summon one, would their aesthetics seem a little bit too tech-ey? I can imagine, for example, a star being appearing in a vessel of some sort or being beamed down into a fight. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure. What say you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T08:51:40-07:00","id":1339193,"title":"","content":"I think you keep thinking that Dreamspeakers = Druids that live in trees.<br /> <br /> Like I said, they freely channel Digital spirits. These fuckers literally sit at a computer and jack in sometimes, and do shit that could make you think they are a virutal adept. There is nothing that says 'you aren't a dreamspeaker cause of this'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T10:24:16-07:00","id":1339628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339026-question-concerning-spirit-allies-guides-for-new-age-dreamspeaker?p=1339179#post1339179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. Not on topic, at least. It's been a while since I did research on occult subjects. I didn't even know Bluefluke released another edition of the Psychonaut Manual until I went looking for links. (The latest I had was from 2015).<br /> <br /> If I had some advice, though, I'd suggest looking up more material on 19th century spiritualism. There's a lot to explore there, because the degree to which occult subjects were part of the mainstream wouldn't be matched until the 60s. Many of the trends that New Age worked with were cribbed from that period. That and the Golden Dawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any further insights in regards to my last question?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T10:52:11-07:00","id":1339632,"title":"","content":"Okay, let's see.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1339026-question-concerning-spirit-allies-guides-for-new-age-dreamspeaker?p=1339191#post1339191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I wanted to represent those as Umbrood extraterrestrial spirits, how do you think I could best do that while still keeping within the dreamspeaker paradigm?<br /> <br /> And if I were to make a pact and summon one, would their aesthetics seem a little bit too tech-ey? I can imagine, for example, a star being appearing in a vessel of some sort or being beamed down into a fight.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure. What say you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have some thoughts.<br /> <br /> First, consider <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automatic_writing\" target=\"_blank\">Automatic Writing</a> being the &quot;interface&quot; between the mage and their alien contacts. It's been used for centuries by various people claiming to have contact with higher or outer beings. From John Dee and Edward Kelly during their formation of the Enochian magic system, to the Spiritualist movement of the 19th century, into early 20th century figures like Aleister Crowley and Sir Arthur Conan Doyle (or rather his wife, with the aid of Harry Houdini), and into the present day with the CIA's Stargate Project and David Icke (the reptllians guy).<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's one of the things that gets forgotten about David Icke. He wasn't just talking about a conspiracy of reptile aliens who secretly control the world. He insists that he learned about said reptilians because of contact he had with spirits/aliens (who also informed him that he was the &quot;Son of the Godhead&quot;).<br /> <br /> Point is, your character's aliens don't need to appear in the flesh. Contact can be indirect, using methods like Automatic Writing to facilitate communication. If you want to be more direct, consider using dreams, visions, and altered states of consciousness to provide &quot;face to face contact&quot;. In which case, the aliens can look however you want (and their forms will likely be distorted or idealized compared to what they &quot;really&quot; look like).<br /> <br /> It's important to remember that a running theme within modern UFOology and related subcultures is the belief that aliens were responsible for myths about ghosts, angels, or other spirits. So an argument could be made that when your character sees the aliens, they look like ghosts or radiant humans all in white. Simply because they figure that's just what they are &quot;supposed&quot; to look like, and it's only primitive humans putting inelegant names to what they didn't understand. The character's fellow Dreamspeakers aren't &quot;wrong&quot;, they just use traditional terminology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 10-05-2019, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T11:12:06-07:00","id":1339643,"title":"","content":"One more thing! If you're looking for official material, World of Darkness: Sorcerer has a section on a Sorcerer society that's a bit up your alley. It's called the Thal'hun, a group of technomancers who revere and emulate a star-hopping alien named Khuvan who they claim taught them their magic. The section on the Thal'hun (p. 36) starts with a recitation of their history, as the Thal'hun know it. That of a race of highly advanced aliens who mastered Thal - the almost magical science derived from sound and vibrations - who, when faced with planet-destroyed calamity, phased their greatest city out of time and space. Meanwhile, 300 of their greatest masters of Thal (the Thal'hun) were converted into beings of pure energy, who could travel the cosmos and be near-immortal. Searching for a new world to phase their great city to, when the time was right. One of those was Khuvon, who taught these Sorcerers the secrets of Thal (and, at least according to the Thal'hun, all other forms of magic previously, albeit in &quot;imperfect form&quot;, hence why it's mystical rather than scientific).<br /> <br /> It's not quite what you had in mind with your character, but I think it could be useful. At least with the opening narration, concerning the alien species.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T16:44:39-07:00","id":1339728,"title":"","content":"The Dreamspeakers' Ghost Wheel Society faction probably have a number of members devoted to exploring the ideas of extraterrestrial and extra dimensional beings as a form of spirit, and all the things associated with them. Ancient astronauts, Blavatskian theosophy, alien abductions/encounters, psychic energy, and various other things mentioned in this thread. While some of the super-traditionalist Dreamspeakers may view them as strange or outlandish, the Society has always been about pushing and breaking boundaries in order to expand the definition of what a spirit is and what the shaman's role is in facilitating (or policing if need be) their interactions with humanity. New Age extraterrestrialism and the like is very much in their wheel house.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}